---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
const lastUpdated = "August 2026";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Editorial Guidelines"
  description="Our detailed process for testing tools, verifying technical documentation, and maintaining independent editorial standards at Pixelquil."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-20">
    <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full bg-brand-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-brand-600">
      Editorial Guidelines
    </span>
    <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 sm:text-5xl">Our Editorial Standards and Technical Process</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Purpose and Mission</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Pixelquil provides privacy focused web tools and technical guides for developers, designers, and site owners. Every tool operates client side in the user browser without transmitting personal data. Our written guides exist to explain the underlying web specifications, security considerations, and optimization techniques behind these utilities.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Testing and Research Standards</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          All technical explanations are developed through direct hands on testing using actual production markup and scripts. We test vector files, code minifiers, and SEO analyzers against current specifications established by official bodies including the World Wide Web Consortium and schema standards organizations.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          When explaining complex topics such as SVG attribute scaling, script sanitization, or metadata validation, our documentation references actual browser rendering behavior across modern engines rather than repeating summary claims from secondary blogs.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Technical Accuracy and Limitations</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We prioritize technical precision over simplified marketing language. If an algorithm relies on an approximation, such as calculating perceived color contrast or vector path conversion, that limitation is explicitly documented on the tool page.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Our team monitors changes to browser APIs, security models, and web standard recommendations to ensure code snippets and instructions remain current.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Peer Review and Community Corrections</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Technical accuracy requires continuous review. Before publishing, content is verified against specification documentation. After publishing, pages are revisited periodically to update code examples or adjust recommendations as browser support evolves.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We actively encourage feedback from developers and designers. If you discover a technical error, broken reference, or outdated code snippet, you can submit a correction notice through our <a href="/contact/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline font-medium">contact page</a>. Reported issues are reviewed and addressed within five business days.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Advertising and Independence</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Pixelquil maintains complete financial and editorial independence. We do not accept paid tool placement, sponsored content, or paid reviews. Tool comparisons and recommendations are determined solely by technical evaluation.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Monetization is limited to automated display advertisements served through Google AdSense. Advertising units are styled to remain visually distinct from site utilities, source code examples, and educational text to prevent accidental clicks and preserve user experience.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>